Daemonarchy project license

This repository (daemonarchy-src) is part of the Daemonarchy project. The project's
repositories, all under https://github.com/jordanhubbard, are:

  daemonarchy          the installer and release engineering
  daemonarchy-desktop  the Daemonarchy look and FreeBSD tools over Omarchy
  daemonarchy-ports    the release ports tree (fork of the FreeBSD ports tree)
  daemonarchy-src      the owned FreeBSD source tree (fork of FreeBSD src)
  omarchy-freebsd      the FreeBSD layer that the x11-wm/omarchy port installs

The map of the repositories is in HACKING.md of the daemonarchy repository:
https://github.com/jordanhubbard/daemonarchy/blob/main/HACKING.md

Daemonarchy-original work in this repository is licensed under the BSD
2-Clause license (SPDX: BSD-2-Clause), whose terms follow. These terms apply
to Daemonarchy project work; no copyright holder is named for that work.

Third-party and upstream-derived components keep their own licenses and
their upstream copyright notices. Which component, at which path, is under
which license is listed in licenses/README.md, and the texts of the licenses
named there are in the licenses/ directory. A file that carries its own license
header or SPDX tag is under that license. The Daemonarchy-original files are
listed in licenses/README.md; any other file in this tree that is not listed
there follows FreeBSD's COPYRIGHT file and the in-tree license files and file
headers that FreeBSD maintains.

The COPYRIGHT file of this repository is unchanged. It states the terms of
FreeBSD as FreeBSD publishes them, and this file does not replace it.

